2|// threadgroup (192 threads) per row. Weights (4 f32) and shared (768 bf16,
3|// expanded exactly to f32) are staged in threadgroup memory with
4|// vectorized 8-byte loads, then each thread weights its 4 consecutive
5|// outputs. Grid is (rows*192, 1, 1), threadgroup (192, 1, 1).
6|//
7|// Reference (slots.py:51-52): (y * weights[..., None]).sum(axis=-2)
8|//   .astype(bf16) + shared, run eagerly as separate kernels, so each
9|//   product is rounded once to f32 and the fold ((p0+p1)+p2)+p3 rounds
10|//   after every add. A single-expression sum lets the compiler contract
11|//   mul+add pairs into FMAs (unrounded products) and breaks bit-exactness
12|//   (starting point: 0/2/2 differ at decode 1/8/32 rows). Here every
13|//   product and every partial sum is assigned in its own statement and
14|//   passed through a volatile register round-trip, which forces the f32
15|//   rounding to materialize; no FMA can form across it. Both bf16
16|//   roundings are kept: bfloat(acc) is the astype, then the bf16 add of
17|//   shared (the staged float is the exact f32 expansion of the bf16
18|//   value, so bfloat(shsh) recovers it bit for bit).
